# Results — ignore large files (weights, checkpoints) but allow small
# benchmark JSON/CSV/PNG so that experiment evidence is committed.
results/*
!results/benchmarks/
!results/benchmarks/*.json
!results/benchmarks/*.csv
!results/benchmarks/*.png

# Generated RFM artifacts — regenerated by scripts, not committed.
# pushcube_canonical/ is ~84MB of episode images+states (collect_pushcube_dataset.py);
# mock_smolvla/ holds mock training weights/configs. LeRobot metadata (info.json)
# under pushcube_lerobot/ IS tracked intentionally.
examples/robot_foundation_models/smolvla/datasets/pushcube_canonical/
examples/robot_foundation_models/smolvla/models/mock_smolvla/

# CI fixture dataset for regression — exception to the data/ rule above.
# ~42KB, 2 episodes, no images. Used by tests/test_rfm_dataset_regression.py.
# Named pushcube_ci_fixture (not pushcube_lerobot_tiny) because it is a
# JSON-only state/action schema fixture, NOT a real LeRobot Parquet dataset.
!examples/robot_foundation_models/smolvla/datasets/pushcube_ci_fixture/
!examples/robot_foundation_models/smolvla/datasets/pushcube_ci_fixture/data/
!examples/robot_foundation_models/smolvla/datasets/pushcube_ci_fixture/data/*.json
